power: supply: bq256xx: no SGM41513 at 0x1a without a charger's registers (issue #225)

Patch 0015 took any answer at I2C 0x1a for the SGM41513 that the ABSSV U30 Air may carry (issue #102). On the
ZTE F50, which has the "ti,bq2560x_chg" node and neither charger, a read at 0x1a does answer, with 0 in every
register: the driver bound a phantom "part 0, rev 0", told it to charge, the fuel gauge reported over-voltage and
the PMIC reset the board about two seconds into the boot - in a loop on a router's USB port (GL.iNet GL-MT3600BE,
Cudy TR3000), not on a computer's (v2026.10.25 and v2026.10.26; the reports are in issue #225).

Before binding, read REG00-REG0A at 0x1a. A real charger holds its reset defaults there (input limit, charge
current, charge voltage, timers), most of them neither 0x00 nor 0xff; with fewer than three such registers this is
not a charger, and the probe ends with "no charger: E (0x1a answers, N of 11 registers set: no SGM41513)". A
charger that answers at the node's address (the SSV U30 Air's SGM41511 at 0x6b) does not come here.

A separate patch on top of 0015, so that a tree already prepared with 0015 takes it as it is.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c
@@ -2124,7 +2124,7 @@
 	bq->bq2560x_chg = of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "ti,bq2560x_chg");
 	if (bq->bq2560x_chg) {
 		struct bq256xx_chip_info *info;
-		int part, err;
+		int part, err, reg, val, nz;
 
 		/* the bq25601 as it is, without a register cache and with its input detection */
 		info = devm_kmemdup(dev, bq->chip_info, sizeof(*info), GFP_KERNEL);
@@ -2151,6 +2151,26 @@
 			if (part < 0)
 				return dev_err_probe(dev, -ENODEV, "no charger: %d (and %d at 0x%02x)\n", err, part,
 						     SGM41513_I2C_ADDR);
+			/*
+			 * Something that answers at 0x1a is not yet a charger. On the F50, which has neither chip, every
+			 * register there reads 0 (issue #225): taken for an SGM41513, that phantom was told to charge
+			 * and the PMIC reset the board, over and over on a router's USB port. A real charger holds its
+			 * reset defaults in REG00-REG0A (input limit, charge current, charge voltage, timers), most of
+			 * them neither 0x00 nor 0xff: fewer than three such registers, and this is not a charger.
+			 */
+			nz = 0;
+			for (reg = 0; reg <= 0x0a; reg++) {
+				val = i2c_smbus_read_byte_data(chip, reg);
+				if (val < 0)
+					return dev_err_probe(dev, -ENODEV, "no charger: %d (0x%02x answers, then %d)\n",
+							     err, SGM41513_I2C_ADDR, val);
+				if (val != 0x00 && val != 0xff)
+					nz++;
+			}
+			if (nz < 3)
+				return dev_err_probe(dev, -ENODEV,
+						     "no charger: %d (0x%02x answers, %d of 11 registers set: no SGM41513)\n",
+						     err, SGM41513_I2C_ADDR, nz);
 			dev_info(dev, "nothing at 0x%02x (%d): the SGM41513 at 0x%02x\n", client->addr, err,
 				 SGM41513_I2C_ADDR);
 			strscpy(bq->model_name, "sgm41513", sizeof(bq->model_name));
